{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25890032",
      "title": "What & Why?",
      "sourceHash": "b4f84cde9d71dbb41cef8471e1788680bbb8e06154dbc2b41e488793663ebf18",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 5.25,
          "en": "So before we get started writing any code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.25,
          "end": 8.44,
          "en": "what actually is testing?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.44,
          "end": 12.42,
          "en": "Well, we did test a lot in this course already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.42,
          "end": 15.6,
          "en": "we did a lot of manual testing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.6,
          "end": 19.5,
          "en": "So that means that we, as a developer, write some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.5,
          "end": 23.52,
          "en": "to implement a certain feature or fix a certain issue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.52,
          "end": 27.13,
          "en": "and then of course, we preview that application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27.13,
          "end": 29.7,
          "en": "in the browser and we test it there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.7,
          "end": 32.82,
          "en": "That's what we do all the time as developers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.82,
          "end": 35.72,
          "en": "that's what we did all the time in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.72,
          "end": 39.86,
          "en": "it's super important because we see what our users will see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.86,
          "end": 41.96,
          "en": "and we definitely wanna polish that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.96,
          "end": 44.04,
          "en": "and make sure that this works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.04,
          "end": 46.77,
          "en": "and that this is not going to go away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.77,
          "end": 51.77,
          "en": "But, testing the app manually is also error-prone,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.03,
          "end": 56.16,
          "en": "at least if it's the only kind of testing you do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.16,
          "end": 58.71,
          "en": "Simply because it's hard to test",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.71,
          "end": 62.17,
          "en": "all possible combinations and scenarios.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.17,
          "end": 64.63,
          "en": "If you have a very complex React app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.63,
          "end": 67.67,
          "en": "with a lot of different pages and features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.67,
          "end": 70.17,
          "en": "and you then add a new feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.17,
          "end": 74.09,
          "en": "or you change an aspect of an existing feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.09,
          "end": 76.77,
          "en": "you will probably test that change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.77,
          "end": 78.63,
          "en": "or that new feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.63,
          "end": 81.25,
          "en": "but you're not going to test all the other parts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.25,
          "end": 83.78,
          "en": "of your application all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.78,
          "end": 86.94,
          "en": "And therefore, you might change something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.94,
          "end": 90.16,
          "en": "which breaks some other feature in your app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.16,
          "end": 93.52000000000001,
          "en": "and since you're not testing everything all the time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.52000000000001,
          "end": 96.96000000000001,
          "en": "that breaking change, that bug,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.96000000000001,
          "end": 101.96000000000001,
          "en": "might slip through and maybe you eventually catch it later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.1,
          "end": 105.78,
          "en": "but that's not guaranteed and you might catch it too late",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.78,
          "end": 108.85,
          "en": "and it might then cause some extra work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.85,
          "end": 113.02000000000001,
          "en": "And that's where automated testing steps in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.02000000000001,
          "end": 117.11,
          "en": "This is not a replacement for manual testing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.11,
          "end": 120.24,
          "en": "manual testing will always be super important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.24,
          "end": 122.08,
          "en": "but it's an addition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.08,
          "end": 127.02,
          "en": "With automated testing, you write extra code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.02,
          "end": 130.21,
          "en": "that runs and tests your other code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 130.21,
          "end": 132.63,
          "en": "your main application code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.63,
          "end": 134.51,
          "en": "And this might sound super weird,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 134.51,
          "end": 137.44,
          "en": "but this is a standard procedure,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.44,
          "end": 141.79,
          "en": "a standard thing to do in modern development.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.79,
          "end": 144.401,
          "en": "And the good thing abut that is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 144.401,
          "end": 146.45,
          "en": "that since you write code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.45,
          "end": 150.16,
          "en": "that tests your entire application automatically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.16,
          "end": 154.45,
          "en": "you can always test everything no matter what you changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 154.45,
          "end": 157.13,
          "en": "because you will automatically then test",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 157.13,
          "end": 158.42000000000002,
          "en": "your entire application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 158.42000000000002,
          "end": 161.81,
          "en": "it doesn't cost you a lot of time to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 161.81,
          "end": 165.21,
          "en": "And therefore, you typically write such tests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165.21,
          "end": 168.24,
          "en": "such automated tests that test",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 168.24,
          "end": 171.82999999999998,
          "en": "the different individual building blocks of your app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 171.82999999999998,
          "end": 176.27,
          "en": "but where you then test all those building blocks together,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 176.27,
          "end": 179.22,
          "en": "whenever you make changes to your code basically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 179.22,
          "end": 184.22,
          "en": "Instead of testing only parts of your app from time to time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.7,
          "end": 187.11,
          "en": "And that's therefore very technical,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 187.11,
          "end": 190.46,
          "en": "but it allows you to test everything all the time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 190.46,
          "end": 193.24,
          "en": "and combined with manual testing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 193.24,
          "end": 197.01,
          "en": "that allows you to catch errors way earlier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 197.01,
          "end": 198.92000000000002,
          "en": "and it allows you to write",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 198.92000000000002,
          "end": 202.003,
          "en": "and ship better code in applications.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}